        <mxCell id="header-sub" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#e2e8f0&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;How does an agent get an isolated place to run the code it writes, and what keeps that code away from the cluster?&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;Scope: kubernetes-sigs/agent-sandbox v1beta1 with gVisor on the on-prem K3s, proposal of 2026-10-23 · drawn in full: what the proposal adds (IA-2) · faded: what already runs&lt;br&gt;Out of scope: the agent&amp;#39;s model and tool calls (AI gateway internals view) · the agent&amp;#39;s identity (zoom 6) · Kata Containers, not available on OpenStack VMs without nested virtualisation&lt;br&gt;Assumed: one namespace of agents per project; the agent itself runs in a long-lived Sandbox and asks short-lived ones for code; warm pool of 1 on the 4 GB budget&lt;br&gt;v0.1 · source: cnp-docs/architecture/cnp · agent-sandbox.sigs.k8s.io (API reference, Python client), github.com/kubernetes-sigs/agent-sandbox&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#94a3b8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
